<!--
  Deliberately NO `package="..."` attribute here, even though this
  module's Kotlin package (com.kbachnative, see KbachModule.kt) differs
  from its Gradle build.gradle `namespace` (com.kbachnative.nativemodule)
  — adding one here to help React Native's autolinking guess the right
  Kotlin package (see react-native.config.js at this package's root, which
  fixes that instead) breaks the actual Gradle build on AGP 9+: it now
  hard-errors ("Setting the namespace via the package attribute in the
  source AndroidManifest.xml is no longer supported") whenever the
  manifest's package doesn't match the namespace exactly. If you're
  tempted to add one back to fix an autolinking symbol-resolution error,
  fix react-native.config.js's packageImportPath/packageInstance instead.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" />
